multiple-choice inference for https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF

    llm.decide(state, "did the deployment succeed?", ["yes", "no", "unclear"])
    -> {"yes": 0.91, "no": 0.03, "unclear": 0.06}

    jev_v1   read the odds off the next token
    jev_v2   grammar, greedy, no odds
    plain    unconstrained

    $ make bench

    mode          accuracy   s/item
    -------------------------------
    jev-v1          94.8%     0.49
    jev-v2          94.8%     0.34
    plain           89.7%     0.37
    any + think    100.0%     3.5

v1 and v2 agree on every item. thinking is 10x slower.


References:

- OpenJev, the same idea on a 4B model: https://github.com/TheoLeeCJ/openjev
- Jev, the closed service it reproduces: https://typesafe.ai
- Qwen3.8-27B: https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B
